  "notes": "A jazz-pianist-turned-R&B producer and The-Dream's principal co-producer; the research windows him 2005–2010 and gives \"63–100 straight; the 2007–09 R&B is 63–75 half-time\", so the felt band is the base with `halfTime` true and the mode at 70. The drum deltas are deliberately small, because the research says why they are: the bed is \"half-time 808 R&B — 808 kick with the space at beat 3, clap/snare on 3, offbeat 808 hats — **kept simple so the chord bed can be complex**\". So the kick carries `lockTo808` 0.6 and a 0.18 tresillo lean, the clap stacks on beat 3 on a dead-flat grid, the hat lane falls to 0.08 fill density, `fills` are pushed to sixteen bars, and the offbeat motion is a shaker/rim perc pair. This is a true 808 model: \"808 sub on roots with slides, long decay, sitting under a full piano voicing\" — so `drums.bass808` takes role `bassline` and there is no `bassline` block. The identifying parameter is the harmony, and the research states it as the division of labour: \"**jazz harmony over an R&B floor** is the parameter — classical piano foundation plus a jazz performance career, so expect 7ths, 9ths, 11ths and genuine voice-leading rather than 2-chord drones\", with \"Los supplies the harmony and Nash the melodic repetition\". So `maxChords` is 6, the triad share is 0.06 — the lowest in this whole section — ninth exceeds seventh, `susOrDimProb` is raised and a passing `vii°` family is authored, while the melody is authored as the repetitive half: a 0.84 step share, `twoBarCellRepeat` and a 3–5 pitch motif. ⚠ Confidence is medium: training, role and credits are sourced, and \"the harmonic claim follows from the sourced jazz background\" rather than from a transcription. ⚠ Every velocity and density number is INFERRED. ⚠ `session.keys` is INFERRED: the entry's Keys line gives \"**jazz harmony over an R&B floor** is the parameter — classical piano foundation plus a jazz performance career, so expect 7ths, 9ths, 11ths and genuine voice-leading rather than 2-chord drones\" and enumerates no tonic, so the values here and their weights are this author's reading of that line.",
